From 28181ee592fd90ae5b731705c9d4c27a2b3485a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Geramy Loveless <geramy.loveless@amd.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 12:15:57 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [Loom] Document the recurrent fork contract and prefix cache
 limits

A text program that updates recurrent state in place must handle the first
span after a fork. The runtime gives a forked row a private writer slot and
keeps the shared slot as an immutable reader, and it does not copy the slot.
A program that reads only the writer slot attends to stale state after every
prefix cache or session hit. The contract was visible only in the fixture
README and the tiny text example.

Describe the encode_state record layout and the first-span rule in the model
program guide. State that a prefix hit ends at a retained boundary, that
session_cache_capacity serves named sessions, and that prefix endpoints are
shared by all requests.

Documentation only.
